     An equal attraction at Scott Fetzer is Ralph Schey, its CEO=20
for nine years.  When Ralph took charge, the company had 31=20
businesses, the result of an acquisition spree in the 1960s.  He=20
disposed of many that did not fit or had limited profit=20
potential, but his focus on rationalizing the original potpourri=20
was not so intense that he passed by World Book when it became=20
available for purchase in 1978.  Ralph=92s operating and capital-
allocation record is superb, and we are delighted to be=20
associated with him.

     The history of the Scott Fetzer acquisition is interesting,=20
marked by some zigs and zags before we became involved.  The=20
company had been an announced candidate for purchase since early=20
1984.  A major investment banking firm spent many months=20
canvassing scores of prospects, evoking interest from several. =20
Finally, in mid-1985 a plan of sale, featuring heavy=20
